  "kp116-img-01.jpg": { headers: ["Topic", "\"Soil Science for Regenerative Agriculture\"", "PQNK – The Natural Blueprint"], rows: [
    ["1. Soil Structure & Water Management", "Recommends mulching and cover crops.", "Mandates permanent raised beds to prevent waterlogging, oxygen depletion, and drowning of microbes. Nature separates aquatic and terrestrial ecosystems—we must too."],
    ["2. Transition Strategy", "Suggests no-till and cover crops.", "Prescribes a one-time subsoiling + Jantar (deep-rooted cover crop) to break hardpan, create pores, and establish microbial habitat. After that, only crop residue and root retention maintain the ecosystem."],
    ["3. Perennial System Design", "Focuses on annual vegetables and cover crops.", "Promotes perennial alley cropping with fruit trees—no need for repeated planting. Only one initial cover crop is needed; thereafter, the system self-sustains."],
    ["4. Pest & Disease Management", "Mentions beneficial insects and KNF inputs.", "Uses BT bacteria as foundational biocontrol, followed by layered predators (insects → birds). This mirrors natural trophic cascades."],
    ["5. Mineral Nutrition", "Discusses compost and mineral amendments.", "Activates the geological mineral bank already present in soil—no external inputs needed. Three stages: liberation → cycling → perpetual abundance."],
    ["6. Scale & Machinery", "Garden-scale, hand-tool methods.", "Includes scalable machinery to plant through mulch and residues—designed for production agriculture, already field-proven at scale."],
    ["7. Irrigation vs. Moisture Management", "Still references irrigation systems.", "Eliminates irrigation entirely. Manages moisture through OM, mulch, and contour design—no artificial watering."],
    ["8. Economic Valuation", "Measures success in yield (kg/acre).", "Measures success in bio-energetic currency—nutrient density, energy flow, and ecosystem services—not just commodity mass."],
    ["9. Funding & Bias", "May promote commercial products (EM®, kits, etc.).", "Self-funded, non-commercial, zero product bias—follows only true ecosystem science."],
  ] },
